      "programmeDescription": "Natural and Social Sciences (Bèta-gamma) combines natural and social sciences at the University of Amsterdam. Students study a common first year, then specialise in a major while continuing interdisciplinary project work.",
      "comparisonExplanation": "Bèta-gamma combines a shared natural- and social-science foundation with a disciplinary major and interdisciplinary projects. With Earth Sciences, the published plan includes 36 EC of genuine elective space. The table accounts for 174 EC; a complete UCR comparison awaits clarification of the remaining Project 4 entry condition for the 2026 intake.",
