      "componentNotes": {
        "uva-58848": "One of two mathematics variants. This illustration retains the Mathematics B variant for natural-science preparation.",
        "uva-58713": "Introduces social-scientific perspectives on states, power and society.",
        "uva-57158": "Develops programming in Python and examines AI and society. Academic-skills assignments are integrated into the current course.",
        "uva-60890": "Studies the origins and development of the universe and life. The current course carries 9 EC.",
        "uva-57369": "Introduces cognition across disciplinary perspectives. The current 6 EC course includes academic-skills work.",
        "uva-58648": "Introduces research methods and the analysis of scientific research. Students must have followed it before Project 1.",
        "uva-58454": "A required 3 EC philosophy-of-science course.",
        "uva-61112": "Studies urban life through disciplinary and interdisciplinary perspectives.",
        "uva-58767": "Studies emergence across scientific domains. Mathematics, natural-science and programming foundations provide preparation.",
        "uva-60749": "Students develop and conduct multidisciplinary research and present it at a symposium. Entry requires having followed the first-year research-methods course.",
        "uva-61107": "Analyses interdisciplinary research and prepares for Project 4. Entry requires passing Project 1.",
        "uva-58560": "One of two practice-project choices. Students develop sustainability advice for an external organisation; the other choice is Placemaking.",
        "uva-58666": "A compulsory Earth Sciences course on plant–soil interactions. Major entry requires at least 48 EC from the Bèta-gamma first year.",
        "uva-59720": "A compulsory practical course, including fieldwork and reporting. Passing its fieldwork and field-report components prepares for Desertification.",
        "uva-59732": "A required 3 EC introduction to programming in R.",
        "uva-58607": "A required 3 EC remote-sensing course. Its attendance requirement must be met before Digital Earth.",
        "uva-58645": "A required Earth Sciences course on food systems and ecosystems.",
        "uva-59727": "A required course on water-related Earth-system challenges.",
        "uva-58797": "A required 3 EC course. Entry requires meeting the Remote Sensing attendance requirement; its own attendance requirement must be met before Desertification.",
        "uva-58921": "A required 3 EC course on developing evidence from data.",
        "uva-58813": "Includes fieldwork. Entry requires passing the Plant-Soil Practical fieldwork and field-report components, or the specified earlier equivalent, and meeting the Digital Earth attendance requirement.",
        "uva-59729": "A compulsory Earth Sciences course in water management.",
        "uva-58949": "A 6 EC research-design course alongside the bachelor project. The formal rules apply the Future Planet Studies entry conditions to Bèta-gamma major students: completion of the first year and at least 42 EC from year two.",
        "uva-58527": "An 18 EC supervised individual research project and thesis. Bèta-gamma students follow the Future Planet Studies entry conditions and must choose an Earth-science topic. The general requirement is completion of the first year and at least 42 EC from year two.",
        "uva-open-electives": "The Earth Sciences plan leaves 36 EC for genuine electives. At most 12 EC may be at any bachelor level; the remaining space uses second- or third-year courses. A completed official Dutch minor can replace these level conditions. Courses must avoid excessive overlap; other arrangements require written examination-board approval."
      }
    }
